		{
			"id": "code_group",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Codes** (35) — Ctrl+hover a link to preview\n\n- [[L1-C03]] — practice needed to break modelling resistance\n- [[L1-C04]] — mapping case study to notation is hardest start\n- [[L1-C07]] — lecturer sees students wait for teacher to start\n- [[L1-C11]] — semantics struggle plus breaking the ice\n- [[L2-C08]] — lecturer sees semantics and refinement as main breakdown points\n- [[L2-C09]] — lecturer sees students stall when identifying actors and actions\n- [[L2-C10]] — worked examples do not transfer when domain changes\n- [[L3-C02]] — large cohort taught with multi-person teaching team\n- [[L3-C14]] — lab assistants break problems into smaller modeled pieces\n- [[L3-C15]] — autonomy first; whiteboard demo when majority stuck\n- [[L3-C16]] — lab supports learning but does not replace theory\n- [[S3-C04]] — earlier courses were shallow crash courses\n- [[S3-C05]] — prior BPMN contact made MSP easier\n- [[S3-C06]] — could start MSP exercises without waiting\n- [[S3-C17]] — one-week BPMN then course moves on\n- [[S4-C03]] — less confident starting without teacher example\n- [[S4-C04]] — worked examples teach reasoning not memorizing shapes\n- [[S4-C05]] — comparing detail levels showed what good enough means\n- [[S4-C06]] — personal quality checklist learned from feedback\n- [[S5-C04]] — drafts version one without waiting for demo\n- [[S5-C07]] — small prototype settles modelling disagreements\n- [[S5-C14]] — wants weekly assessed diagram peer reviews\n- [[S7-C02]] — simple board example then class bullet-list\n- [[S7-C03]] — classmates copy the board instead of trying\n- [[S7-C04]] — starts fast to survive random board pick\n- [[S7-C05]] — teacher stays quiet until students debate\n- [[S8-C01]] — bachelor project required models without teaching them\n- [[S8-C03]] — underlines requirements then pencil-to-pen sketch\n- [[S8-C04]] — examples help notation more than expected answer\n- [[S9-C01]] — Covid online classes made shared modelling messy\n- [[S9-C02]] — teacher solves first then explains notation and why\n- [[S9-C03]] — needs to see it done once before starting alone\n- [[S10-C07]] — stays quiet at the board even with a ready solution\n- [[S10-C08]] — small public doubts go unresolved\n- [[S10-C14]] — desk walk-around beats raising a hand",
			"x": 540,
			"y": 180,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 1060,
