		},
		{
			"id": "memo_group",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Memos** (10) — Ctrl+hover a link to preview\n\n- [[S3M1]] — earlier BPMN contact unlocks MSP start\n- [[S4M2]] — worked examples unlock reasoning and granularity\n- [[L1M1]] — breaking the ice is the main teaching hurdle\n- [[L2M1]] — getting started independently is the hard part\n- [[L3M4]] — scaled labs: autonomy with timed rescue\n- [[S5M3]] — early sharing and self-initiated drafts replace waiting\n- [[S7M1]] — board labs split starters from copiers\n- [[S8M1]] — modelling arrived as a project requirement first\n- [[S9M1]] — start waits on seeing it done once\n- [[S10M2]] — reserved starter: notebook yes, board no",
			"x": -330,
			"y": 180,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 360,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "explainer",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "What this means\n\nStudents often freeze before drawing anything unless a demo, prior example, or taught path is available. That gate can also be a project that requires models before anyone teaches them. Wait-to-start can describe the room (copiers) without describing every student — some start immediately, including reserved students who work in a notebook rather than at the board.",
			"x": 80,
			"y": -300,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "1"
		}
